Yes, that happens. You must consider all factors to survive possible
or actual situations. In this case (foes with wands) the "flee" factor
should have got some priority. In some cases, though, it's impossible;
you encounter some critter, he will be able to follow you, and you've
yet no means to leave the location or level (teleport, digging, etc.).
Yes, that's Nethack; you cannot solve every situation you probably
encounter in some game, you can just maximize your survival probability
given the already present factors, the fixed factors in Nethack, and
the knowledge of provbabilities of the possible random factors.

